{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfact={\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@fact-recovery-value-handling-family\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"In the captured EPaxos package the value a recovery adopts is not protected by the quorum that holds it: four distinct mechanisms of the same recovery path each let a recovering replica end up proposing, and then deciding, a value other than the one its prepare replies carry. (a) startRecoveryForInstance fabricates a value ballot for its own empty state, so the adoption loop skips genuine replies (epaxos/epaxos.go:1145-1165, 1239-1246). (b) A reply whose value ballot is at most the fabricated one is ignored even when it reports the highest accepted value, so a NOOP replaces an accepted value, including one another live replica has already committed. (c) A reply that reports the instance COMMITTED is discarded once its status reaches lb.status, because the pre-accept guard then rejects the remaining replies, so the first recovery attempt stalls until the retry (epaxos/epaxos.go:870-881, 1255-1313). (d) A reply that carries no command decodes as a non-nil empty slice, which the sub-case 5/6 fallback passes to startPhase1 instead of state.NOOP() (epaxos/defs.go:228-235, epaxos/epaxos.go:1307-1311), and which command is adopted is fixed by the replies present when the slow-quorum trigger fires, so arrival order alone can decide whether the owner's command survives. Recovering replicas that already hold the value are not affected by (a)-(b), and the client re-offer protects the single-NOOP case but not the empty-slice case.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"N=5, F=2 configuration of the captured snapshot with Thrifty on and IsLeader false at the recovering replica; the instance owner fails inside its accept window and the recovering replica holds the instance without its command, or (for the arrival-order variant) recovers its own instance while replies at the same value ballot differ.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-decl-recovery\\\",\\\"s-recovery-init\\\",\\\"s-prepare-reply-adopt\\\",\\\"s-subcase-dispatch\\\",\\\"s-preaccept-reply\\\",\\\"s-prepare-reply-unmarshal\\\",\\\"s-commit-repropose\\\",\\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\"],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"2b0dd5bd3ea84bdeba83de7f4c680c00-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":3,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"empty slice adopted and passed through with the trigger timing deciding the command\\\"},\n            {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"cbbf11dd38d843f1b6acf52fd5b6e82e-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":3,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"COMMITTED status adopted then later replies discarded\\\"},\n            {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"ed76b573b9fe4bde9565d4b4678cda85-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":2,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"a recovery lacking the command can decide a different value than a live replica's committed value\\\"}],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"143e14592eea4c42b3c81044e3860348\\\":[7,8,9,11,14,16,17,19,20,21,22,23],\n               \\\"d80cbfd9f9a547639811aeacb19c0a30\\\":[6,10,11,16,19,21,24,25,26,27],\n               \\\"e89ecb076e8d4a78b174f848562ed77f\\\":[6,13,20],\n               \\\"098ab4425325464192aa558be557f0ce\\\":[3,4]}}\nupd={\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Closed the empty-command question's disposition and recorded a synthesis Fact for the recovery-value handling family, so the four defects this run asserts share one navigable statement with their distinct responsibilities and receipts. No measurement changed.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[fact],\n \\\"investigations\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"0757162a4aa64ef4a58a90002641eb27-question-0\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\n   \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"The adoption loop takes any reply whose VBallot is at least the running candidate ballot and copies its command into the candidate, so a reply at the same value ballot that carries no command can replace the command the owner itself contributed; because the dispatch fires when the appended replies reach the slow quorum, which reply is adopted last depends on arrival order, and with two empty replies against one command-carrying reply two of the three exercised orders lose the command while the third keeps it.\\\",\n   \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Whether the remaining three permutations of the three peer replies behave as the trigger position predicts, and whether a scenario with more command-carrying replies than empty ones flips the outcome.\\\"}]}\njson.dump(upd,open('draft/update36.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission update36.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
